{{!-- ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     WHICH NAVBAR
     One bar for the whole site. What changes is how it BEHAVES when the reader
     scrolls — the one difference worth a variant. Shape (centred links, mark
     left, controls right) is decided once in nav/bar.hbs, never per page.

     Four behaviours, each a class the design system already understands:

       full width        a plain bar across the page, sticky, always there
       island            the floating pill, sticky from the first pixel
       island on scroll  full width at rest, drawing itself into the island once
                         the page has moved  (the default)
       hide on scroll    full width and sticky, gone on the way down, back on
                         the way up

     Picked site-wide in Ghost Admin → Design → Site-wide → Navbar style.

     A post or page overrides it with an internal tag — for the landing page
     that wants no chrome, or the long read that wants the bar out of the way.
     The tag always beats the setting:

       #navbar-normal · #navbar-island · #navbar-morph · #navbar-reveal
       #navbar-fixed    (the island, pinned rather than sticky)
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
{{#is "post, page"}}
	{{#post}}
		{{#has tag="#navbar-normal"}}{{> nav/bar shell="nav-shell-full"}}
		{{else has tag="#navbar-island"}}{{> nav/bar}}
		{{else has tag="#navbar-morph"}}{{> nav/bar shell="nav-shell-morph"}}
		{{else has tag="#navbar-reveal"}}{{> nav/bar shell="nav-shell-full nav-shell-reveal"}}
		{{else has tag="#navbar-fixed"}}{{> nav/bar shell="nav-shell-fixed"}}
		{{else}}{{> nav/chosen}}
		{{/has}}
	{{/post}}
{{else}}
	{{> nav/chosen}}
{{/is}}
